---
title: A message from publish to ack (LISTEN / NOTIFY wake-up)
---
sequenceDiagram
    %% Web app: app/routes/publish.py. SQL: app/broker/messages.py.
    %% Wake-up: app/notifier.py (one LISTEN connection per worker). Consumer loop: app/consumer.py.

    participant Browser
    participant App as Web app
    participant DB as Postgres
    box Worker container
        participant N as Notifier (LISTEN connection)
        participant C as Consumer
    end

    N->>DB: LISTEN broker_messages, broker_control

    Note over C: Idle loop: read notifier.version first,<br/>so a NOTIFY that arrives during the claim is not missed
    C->>DB: CLAIM
    DB-->>C: no row
    C->>N: wait for a newer version (at most 1 s, then claim again anyway)

    Browser->>App: POST /publish
    App->>DB: PUBLISH: INSERT ... SELECT FROM generate_series(1, count)
    Note right of DB: trigger messages_notify_insert:<br/>pg_notify('broker_messages', queue), held until commit.<br/>Identical notifications in one transaction are merged,<br/>so a bulk insert sends one
    DB-->>App: count, first_id, last_id (committed)
    App-->>Browser: 303 See Other, /publish?notice=Published ...

    DB-)N: NOTIFY broker_messages (delivered after commit)
    N->>C: version + 1, wake up

    C->>DB: CLAIM (FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED)
    DB-->>C: message (status=processing, locked_by=C, attempts=1)
    activate C
    Note over C: handle the message (the demo sleeps work_ms).<br/>Meanwhile the worker's heartbeat renews the lease every second
    alt handler succeeds
        C->>DB: ACK: status = done
    else handler raises
        C->>DB: NACK: pending again after 2^attempts s, or dead at max_attempts
        Note over C,DB: A delayed retry sends no NOTIFY: the consumer's 1 s poll picks it up
    end
    deactivate C

    loop htmx, every 1 s
        Browser->>App: GET /partials/stats
        App->>DB: queue statistics
        DB-->>App: counts per queue and status
        App-->>Browser: HTML fragment
    end
